<title>MOROCCO: Morocco sells 'Splendid' hotel at $34,000.</title>
<headline>Morocco sells 'Splendid' hotel at $34,000.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco on Friday announced the sale of the 'Splendid' hotel at a symbolic price of 300,000 dirhams ($34,000), as part of its privatisation programme launched in 1993, the privatisation ministry said.</p>
<p>With its 17 rooms, the Splendid hotel was ceded to a group of Moroccan nationals. It is located in Sidi Slimane, 100 km north of Rabat.</p>
<p>It is the 45th state-owned unit to go under the hammer since the government started its privatisation programme in November 1993. A group of 73 other entreprises is expected to be sold by end-1998.</p>
<p>-- Rabat newsrrom (212-7) 726518</p>
</text>
